    {
      "id": "vblA",
      "code_hash": "d8dc1cb53c568244d0dfb5fe9fa85232",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h1 id=\"1-duplicate-card-payments-from-a-delta-table\">1. Duplicate card payments, from a Delta table</h1>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Say you're on the payments team. A customer was charged twice for the\nsame coffee, and by the time support hears about it, they've already\ntweeted. You want to catch these double charges, the same card paying\nthe same amount at the same merchant twice within five minutes, and\nrefund them first.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The rule comes from the <a href=\"https://github.com/AlexanderNenninger/substrait-lean/blob/v0.8.0/catalogue/INDEX.md\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">query catalogue</a>\n(<code>fin-duplicate-payments</code>). Stream processors write it as an interval\njoin; here it is a self-join on a Delta Lake table of card transactions.\nThe refund queue relies on what you hand it: no pair twice, no charge\nmatched with itself, and nothing left over when a charge is reversed.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">We'll go through the whole job:</span>\n<ol>\n<li>read the transactions from a Delta table, with its Change Data Feed;</li>\n<li>write the rule in Ibis and state its contract: what it assumes about\n   the input and what the refund queue may rely on;</li>\n<li>have the checker prove the contract before any data runs;</li>\n<li>run the checked plan on DuckDB and Polars, and see the\n   SQL a warehouse would run (<a href=\"https://github.com/AlexanderNenninger/substrait-lean/blob/main/docs/stability.md#engines\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">the engines</a> says what each\n   engine runs and which SQL sverify writes);</li>\n<li>maintain the result from the change feed when new transactions arrive\n   and old ones are reversed, next to the usual \"process the new rows\"\n   job;</li>\n<li>write the result to a Delta table that carries the contract, so the\n   next job can build on it.</li>\n</ol></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "bkHC",
      "code_hash": "fc29a9877856f2dfd56a4698c044f339",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"1-the-source-a-delta-table-of-transactions\">1. The source: a Delta table of transactions</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Amounts are integer cents, because a DOUBLE amount doesn't compare\nexactly and the rule is an equality of amounts. The table has the Change Data\nFeed on (so later runs can read what changed) and a CHECK constraint\nthat amounts are not negative. The data has one real double charge, a\nnear miss on card 11 half an hour apart, and card 12, whose two payments\narrived without a merchant.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
