    {
      "id": "Kclp",
      "code_hash": "1c7b4061d0ba2126499b64a7f4840831",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>proved</strong></span>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">semantics: reference</span>\n</blockquote>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>postcondition</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>unique(first_txn, duplicate_txn)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.first_txn &lt; _.duplicate_txn)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>_.merchant.notnull()</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.amount_cents &gt;= 0)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.first_ts &lt;= _.duplicate_ts)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>output column</th>\n<th>known values</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>first_txn</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>duplicate_txn</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>card_id</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>merchant</code></td>\n<td>a string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>amount_cents</code></td>\n<td>an integer \u2265 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>first_ts</code></td>\n<td>a timestamp \u2264 2099-12-31 23:59:59.999999</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>duplicate_ts</code></td>\n<td>a timestamp \u2264 2099-12-31 23:59:59.999999</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "emfo",
      "code_hash": "ff114140fae1ca084e762d8cdc6466ab",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">Every postcondition is proved, and no runtime error is possible. Each\none follows from the plan:</span>\n<ul>\n<li><code>unique(first_txn, duplicate_txn)</code>: <code>txn_id</code> is a key of the input, so\n  a pair of ids identifies a pair of rows.</li>\n<li><code>merchant</code> is never NULL, although the column is nullable. Rows join\n  only when <code>a.merchant = b.merchant</code> is TRUE, and <code>NULL = NULL</code> is not\n  TRUE, so card 12's payments never match. pandas' <code>merge</code> matches NaN\n  with NaN, and a Polars join does with <code>nulls_equal=True</code>, so porting\n  this rule to a dataframe library can change its result.</li>\n<li><code>first_ts &lt;= duplicate_ts</code> comes from the join condition, which holds\n  on every output row.</li>\n</ul>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The first refresh reports where each precondition came from:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Hstk",
      "code_hash": "6e924dd06505742dacb11461401add9c",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[\"transactions: unique(txn_id) (checked on data)\", \"transactions: (_.amount_cents >= 0) (Delta constraint)\", \"transactions: (_.ts < datetime(2100, 1, 1)) (file stats @v1)\"]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nWHF",
      "code_hash": "6cda1cace301635679fc0145337230a9",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The amount bound comes from the table's Delta CHECK constraint and the\ntimestamp bound from the file statistics (the maximum <code>ts</code> of each\nfile). The key is checked on the data, since Delta doesn't enforce keys.\nA later batch checks only the files it added.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The node holds the one double charge in the data, without the near miss\nor card 12's merchant-less pair:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "iLit",
      "code_hash": "fc780e700e42f988e5290c3aa2099b1d",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>duplicate_payments</strong></span></span><table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;width:auto;margin:0'><thead><tr><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>first_txn</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>duplicate_txn</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>card_id</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>merchant</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>amount_cents</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>first_ts</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>duplicate_ts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>1</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>10</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>coffee</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>450</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2026-03-02 08:00</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2026-03-02 08:02</td></tr></tbody></table></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZHCJ",
      "code_hash": "69182bad60d1da3a5ac57db8da024cd1",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"break-the-rule\">Break the rule</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">A common bug in a self-join is a row matching itself, which refunds\nevery payment as its own duplicate. Loosen <code>a.txn_id &lt; b.txn_id</code> to <code>&lt;=</code>,\nor drop it, and the checker re-checks the contract:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ROlb",
      "code_hash": "4b80bb040ec206b5e152a39550fecb77",
      "outputs": [
