    {
      "id": "qnkX",
      "code_hash": "368036c5f86ae37af13d4fb84e8afd75",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>proved</strong></span>\n<blockquote>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">semantics: reference</span>\n</blockquote>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>postcondition</th>\n<th>status</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>unique(first_txn, duplicate_txn)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.first_txn &lt; _.duplicate_txn)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>_.merchant.notnull()</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.amount_cents &gt;= 0)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>(_.first_ts &lt;= _.duplicate_ts)</code></td>\n<td>\u2705 proved</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>output column</th>\n<th>known values</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code>first_txn</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>duplicate_txn</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>card_id</code></td>\n<td>any integer</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>merchant</code></td>\n<td>a string</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>amount_cents</code></td>\n<td>an integer \u2265 0</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>first_ts</code></td>\n<td>a timestamp \u2264 2099-12-31 23:59:59.999999</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code>duplicate_ts</code></td>\n<td>a timestamp \u2264 2099-12-31 23:59:59.999999</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "TqIu",
      "code_hash": "d8a5336ecb282d67ec4328da553fb01a",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">With <code>&lt;=</code>, every transaction is its own duplicate, and\n<code>first_txn &lt; duplicate_txn</code> is refused because it is false. With no\ncondition at all, each pair also appears in both orders, and each double\ncharge would be refunded twice. The checker catches both without running\nanything and without test data that contains the bad case.</span>\n<h2 id=\"3-one-plan-every-engine\">3. One plan, every engine</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">You might develop on DuckDB on a laptop and run the job elsewhere in\nproduction. The node's plan is the one Lean checked. Sverify runs it on\neach engine through its own translation, which keeps Lean's semantics\n(NULL keys never match, integers don't wrap around, ties break one way)\nor refuses the plan. Lean's reference profile is the reference, one of\nthe <a href=\"https://github.com/AlexanderNenninger/substrait-lean/blob/main/docs/core-semantics.md#core-profiles-and-engines\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">profiles that refine the core</a>, and\n<a href=\"https://github.com/AlexanderNenninger/substrait-lean/blob/main/docs/stability.md#engines\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">the engines</a> lists which engines run plans, each with a proved\nprofile. With <code>route=\"auto\"</code>, <code>refresh</code> also says how the proof reaches\nthe engine (<a href=\"https://github.com/AlexanderNenninger/substrait-lean/blob/main/docs/guide.md#routes-classes-and-profiles\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\" target=\"_blank\">the guide</a>).\nA node refreshed with <code>engine=</code> has the same rows on each:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "Vxnm",
      "code_hash": "a00353967a5c1e90c11a4c69bc3a6e06",
      "outputs": [
