    {
      "id": "Pvdt",
      "code_hash": "248da36b0ab85e9fe3209d4fcfdbd46b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"4-new-transactions-keeping-the-result-up-to-date\">4. New transactions: keeping the result up to date</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">An hour later, two things have happened to the source table:</span>\n<ul>\n<li>transaction 7 arrived late: card 11 paid 25.99 for books at 09:03, a\n  duplicate of transaction 3, which was loaded in the first run;</li>\n<li>transaction 2 was reversed and deleted, so the coffee pair is no\n  longer a double charge.</li>\n</ul></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "ZBYS",
      "code_hash": "4a0d5c15880b512113b357ddd8a36b43",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "{\"num_added_files\": 2, \"num_removed_files\": 1, \"num_deleted_rows\": 1, \"num_copied_rows\": 5, \"execution_time_ms\": 5, \"scan_time_ms\": 2, \"rewrite_time_ms\": 0}"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "aLJB",
      "code_hash": "e025dc689c2f371ddf7bf3ec38f7c905",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h3 id=\"the-usual-incremental-job\">The usual incremental job</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">The common way to avoid recomputing the self-join is a watermark: find\nthe duplicates among the rows that arrived since the last run, and\nappend them to the output. It is fast and gets both changes wrong:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "nHfw",
      "code_hash": "f933bbfb27e977c120354850f7c9c27e",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "application/json": "[[1, 2]]"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "xXTn",
      "code_hash": "bb7ce8f1b6892d3f5ef5aa156c73a250",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">It misses (3, 7), because transaction 3 is not among the new rows. It\nkeeps (1, 2), because an append-only job never sees the reversal, so a\ncustomer is refunded for a charge that no longer exists. Fixing this by\nhand means joining the new rows with the old ones in both directions and\nhandling deletes and updates. That is the delta rule of a join,\n<code>\u0394(A \u22c8 B) = \u0394A \u22c8 (B + \u0394B) + A \u22c8 \u0394B</code>, which is easy to get subtly wrong.</span>\n<h3 id=\"the-nodes-refresh\">The node's refresh</h3>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>dups.refresh()</code> reads the Change Data Feed from the version the node\nwas computed at, checks the preconditions on the new rows only, and\nruns the delta plans that Lean derived and proved equal to a full\nrecompute:</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "AjVT",
      "code_hash": "337cf4bb3700ff4a5d10b91fecb9bc17",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/plain": ""
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": [
        {
          "type": "stream",
          "name": "stdout",
          "text": "duplicate_payments:\n  route on duckdb: exact; evidence tested at 2.0.0 (facts duckdb-R1, duckdb-R15-int-arith, duckdb-null-keys; #241)\n  transactions@v1\u2192v3: 1 insert(s), 1 delete(s); \u0394 trusted as coming from Delta CDF v1\u2192v3\n  requires transactions: (_.amount_cents >= 0) (Delta constraint)\n  requires transactions: (_.ts < datetime(2100, 1, 1)) (file stats @v3 (new files))\n  requires transactions: unique(txn_id) (checked on data)\n  view duplicate_payments: transactions@v3\n",
          "mimetype": "text/plain"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "pHFh",
      "code_hash": "cc75b8d7449f5aa21a54d8b261d2d608",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/html": "<div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><div style='display: flex;flex: 1;flex-direction: column;justify-content: flex-start;align-items: normal;flex-wrap: nowrap;gap: 0.5rem'><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\"><strong>duplicate_payments after the refresh</strong></span></span><table style='border-collapse:collapse;font-size:0.9rem;width:auto;margin:0'><thead><tr><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>first_txn</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>duplicate_txn</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>card_id</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>merchant</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>amount_cents</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>first_ts</th><th style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>duplicate_ts</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>3</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>7</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>11</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>books</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2599</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2026-03-02 09:00</td><td style='text-align:left;padding:4px 16px 4px 0;white-space:nowrap'>2026-03-02 09:03</td></tr></tbody></table></div><span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The late duplicate is found and the reversed pair is gone, and the node holds the same rows as a new one computed from scratch.</span></span></div>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "NCOB",
      "code_hash": "9396aaa2d85226497e87249985dbf37b",
      "outputs": [
        {
          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><span class=\"paragraph\">The report names the one thing the proof takes on trust: that the change\nfeed turns the old snapshot into the new one (\"\u0394 trusted as coming from\nDelta CDF\"). Where the feed is gone (CDF off, files vacuumed), the\nrefresh diffs the two snapshots and says so. <code>dups.refresh(audit=True)</code>\nalso compares every batch with a recompute before applying it.</span>\n<h2 id=\"5-the-sink-carries-the-contract\">5. The sink carries the contract</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\"><code>dups.write(DeltaSink(...))</code> stores the node in a Delta table, and every\nrefresh writes it exactly once per state: the commit is keyed by the\nsource versions, so a retried job can't write a batch twice. The first\nwrite creates the table, with the proved guarantees as NOT NULL columns\nand CHECK constraints and the plan and contract in the commit metadata.\nLater writes MERGE only the change.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
      "console": []
    },
    {
      "id": "aqbW",
