          "type": "data",
          "data": {
            "text/markdown": "<span class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert contents\"><h2 id=\"what-you-got\">What you got</h2>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">You now have a refund queue you can rely on. The checker proved its\nassumptions before a single row ran and would have caught a self-join\nbug at definition time. The preconditions came from Delta's constraints\nand file statistics where it has them and from the data where it\ndoesn't. The same plan gives the same rows on DuckDB and Polars, and it\nstays right as charges arrive and get reversed, where\nthe watermark job got two rows wrong. The next job builds on the stored\ntable without checking again.</span>\n<span class=\"paragraph\">Next up: <a href=\"?file=02_sensor_alerts.py\">Sensor alerts from an Iceberg table</a>,\nwhere ties and NaN get involved. <a href=\"?file=04_contracts.py\">Contracts</a> and\n<a href=\"?file=05_pipelines_and_engines.py\">Pipelines and engines</a> explain the\nfeatures used here.</span></span>"
          }
        }
      ],
